{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1101771-the-duchy-of-magnolia","id":1101771,"title":"The Duchy of Magnolia?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-08T15:46:42-07:00","id":1101771,"title":"The Duchy of Magnolia?","content":"Is there any official information on the Duchy of Magnolia(Mississippi)? I'm a native of the state and thinking of setting my chronicle there. There's nothing more than the name in C20, so I was wondering if one of the older books might have some concrete data. Any help would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:31:04-07:00","id":1102090,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book here with me to check and make sure, but I'd imagine it would be in Kingdom of Willows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:16:31-07:00","id":1102352,"title":"","content":"Yes, Kingdom of Willows has some info about it. It's one of my favorite entries actually. It's under siege by the duchess of Cotton who is trying to annex it to her own duchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T14:52:12-07:00","id":1102364,"title":"","content":"Cool, I'll have to get that book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:32:42-07:00","id":1102384,"title":"","content":"As much as I was never a fan of the whole &quot;it's all based on States&quot; basis of the game's political geography, I rather wish there'd been an &quot;Atlas of Concordia&quot; sourcebook which gave at least a brief overview of all the Kingdoms and their Duchies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T16:15:41-07:00","id":1102391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1101771-the-duchy-of-magnolia?p=1102384#post1102384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I was never a fan of the whole &quot;it's all based on States&quot; basis of the game's political geography, I rather wish there'd been an &quot;Atlas of Concordia&quot; sourcebook which gave at least a brief overview of all the Kingdoms and their Duchies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except when its not based on states like the Kingdom of Florida.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:06:09-07:00","id":1102637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1101771-the-duchy-of-magnolia?p=1102391#post1102391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except when its not based on states like the Kingdom of Florida.</div> </div> </div> </div>Florida is a state. <br /> <br /> The Kingdom of White Sands is effectively Florida. (Though it's been too long since I've read Kingdom of Willows and don't feel like trying to dig my copy out of storage to see if it actually has a Duchy/Barony/whatever for the panhandle and/or Jacksonville that's separate from White Sands. If anyone actually has a copy of Kingdom of Willows handy, please feel free to clear this up for me.) <br /> <br /> To my knowledge, the only Duchy not based on state borders was the Duchy of Appalachia, and I think the only reason that happened was that Rage Across Appalachia came out three years before Kingdom of Willows. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:29:23-07:00","id":1102646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1101771-the-duchy-of-magnolia?p=1102637#post1102637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Florida is a state.<br /> <br /> The Kingdom of White Sands is effectively Florida. (Though it's been too long since I've read Kingdom of Willows and don't feel like trying to dig my copy out of storage to see if it actually has a Duchy/Barony/whatever for the panhandle and/or Jacksonville that's separate from White Sands. If anyone actually has a copy of Kingdom of Willows handy, please feel free to clear this up for me.)<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, the only Duchy not based on state borders was the Duchy of Appalachia, and I think the only reason that happened was that Rage Across Appalachia came out three years before Kingdom of Willows.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Florida is a state and has 3 Duchies which was what i was getting at. The Duchy of the Dakotas is both states.. and there's no Duchy for Minesota....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}